  "question": {
    "text": "The angle of elevation of the top of a vertical tower from a point A, due east of it is <math><msup><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math> . The angle of elevation of the top of the same tower from a point B, due south of A is <math><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math> . If the distance between A and B is <math><mn>54</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>m</mi></math> , then the height of the tower (in meters), is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>108</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>36</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>54</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>54</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0032_35a62b7cd929.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 267px;\" /></p><p>Let height of the tower be &#39;H&#39;&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;Let <math><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math><br /><math><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></math><br />In&nbsp;<math><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math><br />In <math><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>H</mi></math><br /><br />Since,&nbsp; <math><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;a right-angled triangle.<br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>54</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> &nbsp; &nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo></math>Pythagoras&nbsp;Theorem <math><mo>)</mo></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>54</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>54</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>54</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>H</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>54</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi></math></p>"
  }
